      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1393",
      "html": "<p>Scientific name: Lophiosilurus nigricauda (Mees, 1974). Common name: Jelly Catfish. Family: Pseudopimelodidae. Type locality: Sipaliwini, Suriname.</p><p>Etymology: Greek, lophos = crest + Greek, silouros = cat fish, i.e. crested catfish.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1393",
      "html": "<p>South America: Sipaliwini River basin, Suriname. Also listed for Guyana Waters, Coastal Rivers of Guyanas, Suriname Coastal Rivers and Corintijns.</p><p>IUCN Red List: Least Concern (last assessed 2021).</p>"
    },
    {
